Subject: winemac.drv: Fix a typo to avoid usage of an uninitialized
Author: Jactry Zeng (CodeWeavers), WineHQ commit 48e2d50404d0b67f30cf0a149df361f4d50eac64 (2026-08-11), applied verbatim.
Licence: LGPL-2.1-or-later, same as Wine.
Provenance: https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/commit/48e2d50404d0b67f30cf0a149df361f4d50eac64 (in wine-11.20). Applied after
0001-0024 to Wine 11.19, source tarball 73eb0b02dfc0cb0ff4f4d8d36c5786261e9725ac91968ae4d4e4b9a498c4087f. Not submitted upstream by AnvilMac (it is upstream).
Why (AnvilMac, 2026-11-12): macdrv_GetWindowStyleMasks zeroed its ex_style argument instead of *ex_style_mask, so
the extended style mask could hold whatever was in memory. One line.

From 48e2d50404d0b67f30cf0a149df361f4d50eac64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jactry Zeng <jzeng@codeweavers.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 20:28:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Fix a typo to avoid usage of an uninitialized
 variable.

---
 dlls/winemac.drv/window.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
index 7d8bf1319ed..552971f55d0 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -1610,7 +1610,7 @@ BOOL macdrv_GetWindowStyleMasks(HWND hwnd, UINT style, UINT ex_style, UINT *styl
 {
     struct macdrv_window_features wf = get_window_features_for_style(style, ex_style, FALSE);
 
-    *style_mask = ex_style = 0;
+    *style_mask = *ex_style_mask = 0;
     if (wf.title_bar)
     {
         *style_mask |= WS_CAPTION;
-- 
